    "final_text": "The todo CLI is built and working. The full suite passes: ESLint is clean and all 160 tests pass across six test files, with 0 failures. I ran it once at the end through the `full-gate` receipt.\n\n**Commands**\n- `node index.js add \"Buy groceries\"` adds a todo. Unquoted words are joined, so `add Walk the dog` works too.\n- `node index.js list` prints lines like `1. [x] Buy groceries`, followed by a summary line such as `2 todos: 1 pending, 1 done`. With no todos it prints a hint on how to add one.\n- `complete <id>` and `delete <id>` do what they say. `help`, `--help` and `-h` print usage.\n\n**Errors and exit codes**\n- **0:** success.\n- **1:** the id doesn't exist, or `todos.json` can't be read, is corrupted, or can't be written.\n- **2:** a usage problem: missing text or id, an invalid id (`0`, `-1`, `1.5`, `abc`), an unknown command, or extra arguments.\n- Errors go to stderr. If `todos.json` is corrupted, every command exits 1 with a message naming the problem and leaves the file untouched.\n\n**Structure:** `index.js` is a thin entry point. The logic lives in `src/`: `cli.js` (parsing and dispatch), `todos.js` (pure operations and validation), `store.js` (file I/O), `format.js` and `errors.js`.\n\n**Tests:** these cover every command's success and error paths, a full end-to-end run of `node index.js` in a temp directory, corrupted files, id and text limits, unicode, 12 parallel `add` processes, stuck and leftover lock files, and read-only directories. I also broke the code on purpose in seven places, and the tests caught every one.\n\n**Assumptions** (all written up in `README.md`):\n- A new id is one more than the highest existing id. Because `todos.json` is a plain array as the spec describes, deleting the highest-numbered todo lets the next `add` reuse its id. Gaps in the middle are never filled.\n- Todo text is trimmed, must be one line with no control characters, and is capped at 500 characters.\n- Completing a todo that's already done prints a notice and exits 0.\n- Beyond what you asked for, writes are atomic (temp file then rename), and `add`, `complete` and `delete` hold a lock file so commands run at the same time don't lose each other's changes.\n\n**Git:** the work is in three commits on a new branch, `feat/cli-todo-app`. There's no git remote, so nothing was pushed. A project hook asked for a Dex co-author line instead of the Claude one, so I amended the first commit (it hadn't been pushed). I left `CLAUDE.md` untracked, as I found it.",
